    "community_snippets":  [
                               {
                                   "title":  "Sweet Bean Paste by Durian Sukegawa | Goodreads",
                                   "snippet":  "An elderly woman with disfigured hands and a troubled past, she makes the best sweet bean paste Sentaro has ever tasted. The unlikeliest of friendships blossoms, but it will take all of their resolve - and plenty of pancakes - to protect themselves when Tokue\u0027s dark secret comes to light.",
                                   "link":  "www.goodreads.com/en/book/show/33376821-sweet-bean-paste"
                               },
                               {
                                   "title":  "Sweet Bean Paste by Durian Sukegawa | Goodreads",
                                   "snippet":  "Instead, he works in a tiny confectionery shop selling dorayaki, a type of pancake filled with sweet bean paste. With only the blossoming of the cherry trees to mark the passing of time, he spends his days listlessly filling the pastries. Until one day an elderly, handicapped woman enters the shop.",
                                   "link":  "www.goodreads.com/book/show/36352961-sweet-bean-paste"
                               },
                               {
                                   "title":  "Book Review: Sweet Bean Paste — A Book That Invites You To Listen",
                                   "snippet":  "Durian Sukegawa\u0027s Sweet Bean Paste (originally An) is one of those rare novels that moves you with its silence as much as its words. It\u0027s a tender meditation on purpose, connection, and what it means to live a meaningful life—even when the world refuses to see your worth. The story unfolds like the slow, patient rhythm of making dorayaki: deliberate, humble, and yet full of quiet grace ...",
                                   "link":  "booksandus.com/sweet-bean-paste-review/"
                               },
                               {
                                   "title":  "Book Review: Sweet Bean Paste by Durian Sukegawa",
                                   "snippet":  "A gentle and heartwarming review of Sweet Bean Paste by Durian Sukegawa—on food, second chances, and quiet heartbreak.",
                                   "link":  "kohleyedme.com/2025/06/19/book-review-sweet-bean-paste-by-durian-sukegawa/"
                               },
                               {
                                   "title":  "Book Review - \"Sweet Bean Paste\" - Sci-fi Fantasy Lit Chick",
                                   "snippet":  "Thematically, Sweet Bean Paste focuses on the benefits to friendship and in being honest with ourselves and others. Sentaro tends to keep things to himself and doesn\u0027t like socializing, with Tokue treats their shop\u0027s customers as people with lives and troubles of their own, and she\u0027s never too busy to not lend a compassionate ear.",
                                   "link":  "scififantasylitchick.wordpress.com/2025/07/01/book-review-sweet-bean-paste/"
                               },
                               {
                                   "title":  "Wikipedia: Sweet Bean Paste (novel)",
                                   "snippet":  "[Wikipedia Synopsis] Sweet Bean Paste (Japanese: あん, Hepburn: An) is  a 2013 novel by Japanese author Durian Sukegawa (pen name for Tetsuya Akikawa). It tells the story of an elderly woman, a middle-aged man, and a young girl who come together in an unusual companionship to explore friendship, life, and meaning. The English translation, by Alison Watts was published in 2017.",
                                   "link":  "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet%20Bean%20Paste%20(novel)"
                               }
                           ],
